        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "49482944-8312-5206-98ca-19f3eef32570",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Erskine, Earl of Mar; George I of Great Britain\n- Roles: King of Great Britain and Ireland; ruler of Brunswick-Lüneburg (Hanover)\n- Events: Jacobite rebellion; battle of Sheriffmuir\n- Places: Great Britain; Ireland; Brunswick-Lüneburg (Hanover); Holy Roman Empire\n\nFacts:\n- George I of Great Britain was born as George Louis on 28 May 1660 and was also known in German as Georg Ludwig.\n- From 1698, George I ruled the Duchy and Electorate of Brunswick-Lüneburg, also called Hanover, in the Holy Roman Empire.\n- George I became King of Great Britain and Ireland on 1 August 1714.\n- In 1714, the new king deprived John Erskine, Earl of Mar, of office.\n- After losing office in 1714, John Erskine, Earl of Mar, raised the standard of rebellion against the Hanoverians.\n- In November 1715, at the battle of Sheriffmuir, John Erskine, Earl of Mar, commanded forces that outnumbered those of his opponent, but he failed to win a victory.\n- George I remained King of Great Britain and Ireland until his death on 11 June 1727.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
